{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791428814,"nonce":"UUu/zuUa3R5si0DFi7mkmD3h4UQ=","title":"Macro catch-all handlers consume typer deferral as a user error","message":"MacroTypingChecks.hx defines rejects(e) as try { Context.typeof(e); false; } catch (error:Dynamic) { true; }. Native Haxe accepts takesInt(12), 2 + 3, string concatenation and a function returning Int. Rayzor answers true for these valid expressions during phase-A expansion and fails with \"valid argument rejected\".\n\nThe interpreter deliberately allows MacroError::NeedsTyper through catch(Dynamic), while a typed haxe.macro.Expr.Error catch propagates the deferral. This can make corpus typeError assertions accidentally succeed without a typing check. Simply propagating NeedsTyper requires stricter deferred typing first, because invalid assignments currently accepted by lowering would otherwise turn into false negatives.\n\nReproducer: /tmp/MacroTypingChecks.hx. Native and Rayzor evidence: /tmp/rayzor-macro-typing-before-v1.log and /tmp/rayzor-macro-typing-errors-v1.log. Scoped privacy and Any probe diagnostics are tracked separately under 7d98b4af7e339634383cc66ebc1bdfe349f7b5ae90c0c9447219b0b133db72c4.","files":null}]}